{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae","id":1109992,"title":"Celestines, Incarnae and the Fae.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T18:41:06-07:00","id":1109992,"title":"Celestines, Incarnae and the Fae.","content":"A great many of themighty spirit beings mentioned in Mage and Werewolf are regularly linked with the fae in those books. However, they are all but nonexistant in Changeling publications.<br /> <br /> With the coming of CtD 20, and the FAR more playable Nunnehi and Menehune, a more comprehensive look at these &quot;Umbrood&quot; is in order.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T18:52:55-07:00","id":1109995,"title":"","content":"I don't like mixing Umbral stuff with Changeling myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:46:50-07:00","id":1110015,"title":"","content":"Well, the Umbra is a different level of Reality from the Dreaming. The spirits of the Umbra do understand the nature of Changelings though, and they approve of them because Changelings are doing their job right while Fera tend to be too filled with Rage to do their job right. In general, however, the spirits of the Umbra will not bother the Kinain. The Nunnehi, Menehune, Hsien, etc are another story all together and will likely be treated with kindness by the spirits of the Umbra because they are relatively peaceful creatures (at least in the eyes of the spirits of the Umbra) because they lack Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T03:16:56-07:00","id":1110110,"title":"","content":"I very much agree, as I've said before I think the Deep Umbra and Deep Dreaming are the same place must different perspectives.<br /> <br /> We need more on Menehune, Nunnehi and Hsien's perspective both on the Dreaming but also on the spirits they deal with's impressions.<br /> <br /> @Aya Tari<br /> From my understanding the spirits seem to be pretty chill with the Fera's work, because if the world isn't Apocalypsed yet someones doing something right, and Rage is apart of the Fera and their Job. Conversely Changelings jobs are essentially to exist... so yeah they are doing that, there's like ten times more of them then say werewolves and they have a more lax jobs and less genocidal enemies and arguably greater centralization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T06:21:29-07:00","id":1110139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1109995#post1109995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like mixing Umbral stuff with Changeling myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, I agree. But if you have Nunnehi and/Menehune in the troupe, the game will involve the Umbra and spirits.<br /> <br /> A simple build system, similar to chimera creation would work. As would some basic stats for animal spirits, elementals and other sorts Changelings might run into.<br /> <br /> More powerful spirits, like Totems and others need attention. Several have obvious connections to the fae. Such as: American Dream, Bacchus, Coyote, Danu, Fox, Owl, Raven, Stag and Unicorn among others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-01-2017, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:12:23-07:00","id":1110268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110015#post1110015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Umbra is a different level of Reality from the Dreaming. The spirits of the Umbra do understand the nature of Changelings though, and they approve of them because Changelings are doing their job right while Fera tend to be too filled with Rage to do their job right. In general, however, the spirits of the Umbra will not bother the Kinain. The Nunnehi, Menehune, Hsien, etc are another story all together and will likely be treated with kindness by the spirits of the Umbra because they are relatively peaceful creatures (at least in the eyes of the spirits of the Umbra) because they lack Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nunnehi and Menehune can step sideways into the Umbra, have spirit guides and totems. They will encounter friendly and unfriendly spirits. <br /> <br /> According to the Fera, the Wyrm is demented because of the Weavers Banal web. Strikes me that there is some powerful story potential there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-02-2017, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T09:41:22-07:00","id":1110580,"title":"","content":"Nunnehi and Nuwisha are not only likely allies, but sound like a great chronicle. Neither have Rage, and would likely have many overlapping allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T14:46:44-07:00","id":1110665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110580#post1110580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nunnehi and Nuwisha are not only likely allies, but sound like a great chronicle. Neither have Rage, and would likely have many overlapping allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuwisha have a Gift to get Rage, though, so all is not smiles and sunshine. They're also likely to be a bit more vicious than most kithain are comfortable, seeing as how they have to keep trying to beat lessons through Garou skulls and all. It tends to starkly color one's world view.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, though, they'd get on about as well with the hsien, I think, if one followed Zhongkui (incorrectly Romanized as Chung Kuel over the correct Wade-Giles form Chung-kuei, because for some reason people though that tapping into the 1e Deities and Demigods book for AD&amp;D, errors, fabrications and all, was a good place for WoD material).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T15:17:10-07:00","id":1110673,"title":"","content":"The gurahl straight up say they often feel they have more in common with the fae than with other Fera. I have found this to often be true within my own games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T16:38:00-07:00","id":1110688,"title":"","content":"In a world where the two exist it's more than bizarre that the vast place that it's the Dream Zone, where not only the dreams of individuals, but also ALL concepts, fantasies, myths, the very essence of nightmares, and all things related to dream can be found, that extends trough all the Umbra...won't have any bussiness with the Dreaming, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Then again, this happens just for the same reason as the inconsistencies between Werewolf and Mage Umbra. Old books tried to be crossover friendly, and portrayed the Dreaming and the Dream as one place perceived by different perspectives. That didn't last, and asking that now would be like asking for a relation between the Wyrm, Oblivion and Entropy. Between the Abys, the Abys and the other Abys. Between Stasis, Banality and the Weaver. This last one I particularly loathe, as (when carelessly done, like, say, in the official material of\u00a8 the Nunnehi) fills Changeling with Werewolf assumptions, like: &quot;Urbane it's more Banal than the wyld forest. AKA: Man BAD, Tree GOOD&quot; which should not be the case, never, ever.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, if you're going to have players stepping sideways you shouldn't have to read other publications. A Changeling book or section about the Umbra wouldn't be bad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-02-2017, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T18:05:50-07:00","id":1110710,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah virgin idyllic wilderness should never have any sort of connection to pure glamour then the slums of s a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:18:14-07:00","id":1110813,"title":"","content":"If you don't want to tear apart the strong relation between the fae and the dreams of humans, transforming them in naturae, then it would be much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Werewolf may be played without humans being too important, but Changeling looses a lot of it's glamour if you don't have to fight to make humans dream and fantasise, instead retiring to your not-Caern to fight against the <s>Wyrm/Weaver</s> Banality of humans that wants to contaminate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:21:55-07:00","id":1110838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110813#post1110813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't want to tear apart the strong relation between the fae and the dreams of humans, transforming them in naturae, then it would be much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Werewolf may be played without humans being too important, but Changeling looses a lot of it's glamour if you don't have to fight to make humans dream and fantasise, instead retiring to your not-Caern to fight against the <s>Wyrm/Weaver</s> Banality of humans that wants to contaminate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As stated in the initial, and subsequent posts the Nunnehi and Menehune are mentioned. And games that include them will go into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Also- Many totems have connections with the Western fae, like Stag. So why not have a look at these?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-03-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:52:09-07:00","id":1110848,"title":"","content":"CtD and WtA are natural crossovers, as the Changelings and the Fera have a number of common concerns and common enemies, especially when it comes to the Nunnehi and the Fera. While people might not like the conflicts of Urban versus Rural or Man versus Nature, it is well established in oWoD that humanity causes many problems in the world because of their destruction of the natural world and because of their willingness to prey on their own kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:56:48-07:00","id":1110853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110673#post1110673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gurahl straight up say they often feel they have more in common with the fae than with other Fera. I have found this to often be true within my own games</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this statement flat out doesn't make sense on a number of levels, and could be taken to be in-character hyperbole. Gurahl are still Ragebeasts, even if they're less likely to frenzy and eat you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:49:22-07:00","id":1110898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110838#post1110838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As stated in the initial, and subsequent posts (if you bother to read them), the Nunnehi and Menehune are mentioned. And games that include them will go into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Also- Many totems have connections with the Western fae, like Stag. So why not have a look at these?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you clearly bothered to read my posts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph, in post #10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, yeah, <b>if you're going to have players stepping sideways</b> you shouldn't have to read other publications. <b>A Changeling book or section about the Umbra wouldn't be bad</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying that Werewolf may damage the themes of changeling if crossovered without caution, thus,<b> for this very reason, including a section about the Umbra in Changeling it's a good Idea</b>, because that way you don't need to read Werewolf and you can focus on the themes of Changeling, on how faes interact with these beings. It would also be great to do this with as much care for the themes of Changeling as possible.<br /> <br /> Why not have a look at Totems?. Why not have a look at Oneira, Demesnes, The Gateway to Arcadia, The Dream Zone?. I'm not against your idea just because I don't want it to focus strictly on the Garou Nation, nor because I would prefer it to cater to the worldview and themes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that the Nunnehi could be improved by making them less werewolvish and more like their occidental cousins (who are likely to be more related to Stag than the native american faes, if you want to go there), which does not mean in any way that they have to dispense with the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T14:57:57-07:00","id":1111024,"title":"","content":"The Oneira are something I was hoping to go into. In my home games, one of them known as Lord Somnus was a powerful force. I statted him much like a powerful fae with both potent Redes and high Arts and Realms. Much like a Dreaming version of an Umbrood Preceptor. He was immune to cold iron, like a fomorian.<br /> <br /> On that note- I could see the Fomorians being Umbrood rather than Fae. Hence their immunity to iron and great power.<br /> <br /> Do you think Totems should be available to Western fae? They are not so different from Noble Houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-04-2017, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T17:49:07-07:00","id":1111079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110898#post1110898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [B]Because you clearly bothered to read my posts.[B]</div> </div> </div> </div>Aleph- I apologize. I thought you were actually different commenters, as I am reading and commenting on a phone at work. Bad form on my part. I took offense from my own muddled data and foolishness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-04-2017, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:16:53-07:00","id":1111295,"title":"","content":"No problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think Totems should be available to Western fae? They are not so different from Noble Houses.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand Changeling's authors desires to keep Umbra references low...I think it's a shame to have pacts between werewolves and faes, especially one so strong as the one with the Fianna, that allows them to learn a Gift that call faes to their aid, and yet say that Western fae (the ones that almost surely did the pact, as Fianna are a western tribe) have no contact with the Umbra at all. Does this mean that they should have Totems?-I think it should be rare, but not unheard off.<br /> <br /> Shamanic like practices weren't nonexistent in Eurrope, even taking Garou out of the equation. Shamanic Mages can have a Totem on the grounds of ancient pacts made by ancient mages even if they aren't american. And a strong enough trust between faes and spirits to justify having the latter teach a Gift that forces fae to come to the caller's aid screams &quot;ancient pacts&quot;. Fae may have forgotten much of this but surely Stag remembers...so, yeah, I believe that western faes could have ancient pacts with Stag and perhaps a few other potent spirits of the dreams. These pacts could be used to justify the Totem background, albeit I would recomend to take a different aproach to it's rules, much like Mage's Totem it's not exactly the same as Garou Totem.<br /> <br /> To put it otherwise, if <b><i>mages </i></b>can have totems, then I don't see why deny them to any other living being, as long as they are treated in a way that's coherent with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:14:58-07:00","id":1111327,"title":"","content":"European Shamanism is very interesting. Finnish and Slavic traditions in-particular have a wonderful narrative feel. Muxh of this trickles down into Germanic fable. Good reading.<br /> <br /> Totems could be an interesting means of patronage for Kinain and Enchanted mortals. The boons of totems are not that different from Bestowements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:11:36-07:00","id":1111723,"title":"","content":"This is the sort of spirit being that I thought would be interesting in Changeling. Though I would use such beings sparingly, they would be very interesting in a chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Murica</b><br /> America the beautiful, America the bold, America the brave. Murica is the spirit of National pride in America, and as such represents all that is great and dreadful about the American spirit. This powerful spirit can be a great ally of changelings, and is himself a servant of the American Dream. He was born of the ashes of the many smaller tribal spirits that protected the Native American nations before the Western settlement of the land. As the American people grew, so did America the Beautiful, growing up next to American Dream (a totem spirit) and O\u2019Mighty Dolla, and later Easy Credit. The loyalty of the citizens to their homeland and their nation made him powerful, and his influence stretched from one coast to another. Despite economic hardships and sometimes lack of faith in the country, America the Beautiful always had a hand in pushing patriotism back into the forefront of the nation\u2019s mind. He changed drastically from year to year, becoming more aggressively protective of the country in sync with the citizens.<br /> In recent years, after struggling to maintain belief in the American way of life, he took up the mantle of Murica as a drastic effort. He chose to adopt a symbol of blind patriotism rather than true nationalism to keep people vested in him. These days, Murica urges paradoxes such as fighting for freedom and justice, enforcing military acts to ensure peace, and the rights of citizens to protect their families with weapons. He doesn\u2019t care if the American people fight amongst themselves over what is right and wrong, as long as they have passion for him and the land they live in.<br /> Image: When Murica manifests in the physical realm, he prefers to take on the form of a darkly tanned man wearing blue jeans, a button-down shirt, a large belt buckle, a bolo tie, and a Stetson hat. It talks slowly and precise, but does not have a drawl or any other discernable accent. In the Dreaming, it looks like a waving American flag. He is often seen in the company of Autumn Sidhe, Redcaps and Trolls.<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 7, Perception 6, Intelligence 5, Wits 5<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Intimidation 3, Kenning 5, Melee 3, Stealth (Surprise) 4, Gremayre 5, Science 4,<br /> <b>Health Levels: </b>OK, OK, OK, OK, \u20131, \u20131, \u20131, \u20131, \u20132, \u20132, \u20132, \u20135, Incapacitated<br /> <b>Redes:</b> Cleanse the Blight, Peek, Sense Banality, Shapeshift, Poof Begone, Wellspring, Wyrd<br /> <b>Arts: </b>Autumn 5, Chicanery 5, Legerdemain 5, Naming 5, Oneiromancy 4, Primal 2, Wayfare 3, Soothsay 3, Skycraft 5, Winter 4. <b>Realms: </b>Actor 5, Fae 2, Nature 2, Scene 5, Time 5<br /> Glamour 7, Willpower 8, Banality 3 (Immune to cold iron)<ul><li><b>Peek</b> <b>(varies):</b> Murica can peer from the Near Dreaming to the Autumn world. The spirit spends one point of Willpower and rolls Glamour versus the local Banality. If successful, she can peer into the Near Dreaming, or out of the Near Dreaming into the Autumn World for no cost.</li> <li><b>Poof Begone (costs 1 Glamour): </b>This power is the ability to vanish at one place in the Dreaming and reappear in another. The exact distance is limited, but certain areas of the Dreaming are known to enhance this Rede. For Murica. standing in a parking garage or city dump, increases the maximum allowable distance (by 50 feet). A chimera must be able to see the destination of the Rede. The user could poof anywhere in a house, but he would have to be able to see the house\u2019s exterior, and he could only poof to one of the outer rooms \u2013 not an interior room or the basement. This ability is usable only in the Dreaming, even if the character possesses Wyrd. If Murica is killed or otherwise Undone, he reforms in the Dreaming/Umbra on the next Independence Day.</li> <li><b>Wellspring (varies):</b> The Spirit acts in much the same manner as a Freehold, providing spiritual sustenance for any fae who spent enough time in his company. The Spirit spends two points of Glamour per Freehold level, up to ten points to make a Level 5 holding. For the next lunar month, he is a freehold of that level for all purposes, though he does not have a type. Murica can terminate this power at any time before the end of the month. When it ends, he regains half of the Glamour he invested to become a Freehold.</li> </ul>As a Spirit, Murica has no special vulnerability to Cold Iron, though he can be killed temporarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-05-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:02:59-07:00","id":1112133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1110853#post1110853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that this statement flat out doesn't make sense on a number of levels, and could be taken to be in-character hyperbole. Gurahl are still Ragebeasts, even if they're less likely to frenzy and eat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it's absolutely in character hyperbole. It's from the gurahl's opinion of the fae secton. But the fact that a werebear feels strongly enough to say that must mean that there's something there.<br /> <br /> As for the ragebeast-ness, I personally don't see the issue. Many of the fae are just as brutal, even if theyou don't have supernatural anger issues backing it up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:31:39-07:00","id":1112152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109992-celestines-incarnae-and-the-fae?p=1112133#post1112133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh it's absolutely in character hyperbole. It's from the gurahl's opinion of the fae secton. But the fact that a werebear feels strongly enough to say that must mean that there's something there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that the author of the breedbook mostly wrote for Changeling. Which, whether or not it is the cause of that character's odd words, is the truth of the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the ragebeast-ness, I personally don't see the issue. Many of the fae are just as brutal, even if theyou don't have supernatural anger issues backing it up </div> </div> </div>The anger issues and frenzying make all the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}